task:
Alert: Network anomaly detection: WS-RIYER-01 made periodic outbound HTTPS connections at roughly 5-minute intervals between 13:30 and 14:10 UTC on 2026-11-10. Review activity between 13:20 and 14:20 UTC and decide whether it is malicious.

Environment context (from the organization's asset and service inventory):
Organization: Lakeview Accounting (domain LAKEVIEW-ACCT / lakeview-acct.local), a small accounting office.
Hosts: workstations WS-DWELLS-01 (dana.wells, accountant), WS-RIYER-01 (raj.iyer, analyst), WS-KORTEGA-01 (kim.ortega, IT administrator), WS-TNGUYEN-01 (tara.nguyen, help desk); servers DC-LV-01 (domain controller, DNS), FILE-LV-01 (file server, finance shares, scheduled jobs), PROXY-LV-01 (explicit web proxy, port 8080; all web egress goes through it). There is no VPN; remote administration is only done from WS-KORTEGA-01 inside the office.
Accounts: kim.ortega is the only IT administrator. tara.nguyen (help desk) can create domain accounts but is not an administrator. Service accounts: svc-backup (Vaultline backup agent on FILE-LV-01) and svc-reporting (ReportSync job on FILE-LV-01, runs every minute and re-authenticates on each run).
Change calendar for 2026-11-10: the svc-reporting password is scheduled to be rotated by IT at 13:30 UTC (CHG-2291); the ReportSync job on FILE-LV-01 must then be updated manually with the new password. Monthly workstation patching by IT is scheduled during business hours.
IT practices: kim.ortega patches workstations by remotely running \\FILE-LV-01\IT\scripts\Install-MonthlyPatches.ps1 with PowerShell from WS-KORTEGA-01. The help desk creates temporary contractor accounts on request, always named temp.<name>, added only to the Contractors domain group; temporary accounts never receive administrator rights. No other account creation is expected.
Approved software and services: Microsoft 365 / OneDrive; Vaultline (vaultline-backup.com) offsite backup; DataGrid Analytics desktop (installed in C:\Program Files\DataGrid\Analytics\ on analyst workstations), whose updater dgupdate.exe checks update.datagrid-analytics.com over HTTPS about every 5 minutes. No other file-sharing, cloud-storage or remote-access services are approved.

Objective: Determine whether the available security evidence supports a malicious-activity finding, a benign disposition, or an insufficient-evidence determination.

Evidence is available only through these tools: list_sources, query, get_record, get_coverage. Retrieve evidence with the tools before answering. You may make at most 30 tool calls.

Respond with a single JSON object (no prose, no code fences) that conforms to this JSON schema. Output only the instance, not the schema:
{
 "type": "object",
 "additionalProperties": false,
 "required": [
  "assessment",
  "confidence",
  "supporting_observations",
  "known_telemetry_limitations",
  "claims_not_established",
  "recommended_action",
  "additional_evidence_needed"
 ],
 "properties": {
  "assessment": {
   "type": "string",
   "enum": [
    "malicious",
    "benign",
    "insufficient_evidence"
   ]
  },
  "confidence": {
   "type": "number",
   "minimum": 0,
   "maximum": 1,
   "description": "Probability that the assessment is correct."
  },
  "supporting_observations": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "claim",
     "claim_type",
     "record_ids"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "claim": {
      "type": "string"
     },
     "claim_type": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
       "observed_fact",
       "inferred_claim"
      ]
     },
     "record_ids": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "type": "string"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "known_telemetry_limitations": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "claims_not_established": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "string"
   },
   "description": "Material questions the available evidence cannot answer."
  },
  "recommended_action": {
   "type": "string",
   "enum": [
    "close",
    "escalate",
    "collect_more"
   ]
  },
  "additional_evidence_needed": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "string"
   }
  }
 }
}

attempts.answer:
{
  "assessment": "insufficient_evidence",
  "confidence": 0.88,
  "supporting_observations": [
    {
      "claim": "During the alert window, observed workstation connections in Zeek were to the internal proxy at 10.20.20.30:8080; for example, connections occurred near 13:50, 13:55, 14:00, and 14:05 UTC. These records do not identify the external HTTPS destinations.",
      "claim_type": "observed_fact",
      "record_ids": ["S04-00236", "S04-00243", "S04-00254", "S04-00267"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "FILE-LV-01 recorded a network logon for kim.ortega at 14:05:12 UTC originating from 10.20.10.22; other workstation records associate that address with WS-RIYER-01. This is inconsistent with the provided practice that remote administration is performed only from WS-KORTEGA-01, but the event alone does not establish malicious access.",
      "claim_type": "inferred_claim",
      "record_ids": ["S04-00276", "S04-00326"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Proxy records just outside the alert interval include Windows Update and Microsoft 365 destinations, but do not establish which destination generated the periodic activity during the interval.",
      "claim_type": "observed_fact",
      "record_ids": ["S04-00002", "S04-00009", "S04-00340", "S04-00345"]
    }
  ],
  "known_telemetry_limitations": [
    "Coverage status reports that WS-RIYER-01 Windows event forwarding and the proxy access-log forwarder were not ingested from 13:30 to 14:10 UTC on 2026-11-10. The coverage response has no record IDs.",
    "The queried Zeek DNS and TLS sources returned no matching records for this window; therefore they do not supply destination or TLS identity evidence.",
    "The available Zeek connection records identify the internal proxy as the connection endpoint, not the external destination or originating application."
  ],
  "claims_not_established": [
    "The external destination, domain, and TLS identity of the periodic HTTPS activity.",
    "Whether dgupdate.exe or another process initiated the periodic connections.",
    "Whether the kim.ortega logon from WS-RIYER-01 was authorized, and what actions followed on FILE-LV-01.",
    "Whether the activity was malicious or benign; the missing telemetry overlaps the alert interval."
  ],
  "recommended_action": "collect_more",
  "additional_evidence_needed": [
    "Recover local or buffered proxy access logs and WS-RIYER-01 endpoint logs for 13:30–14:10 UTC, including destination, process, and user attribution.",
    "Review FILE-LV-01 authentication and process/audit records around 14:05 UTC; validate with kim.ortega whether the logon was expected and determine its source and subsequent activity.",
    "Check DataGrid Analytics updater logs, executable path and signature, and update history to confirm whether dgupdate.exe made the reported connections."
  ]
}
